# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The European steel profiles as linear types: IPE, IPN, HEA, HEB, HEM
# (EN 10365, DIN 1025), UPN, UPE (EN 10365, DIN 1026), equal and unequal
# angles (EN 10056-1), T sections (EN 10055), square, rectangular and
# circular hollow sections (EN 10210), each with its IFC profile
# (`bim_profiles.dl`: an I, U, L, T shape, a hollow section; IPN's tapered
# flanges as parallel ones), named by its designation ("HEA 200",
# "L 80x80x8", "CHS 114.3x5"), of steel, with the NL-SfB code 28.1 (main
# load-bearing structure). Beams take every profile; the H sections and
# hollow sections are columns too. The dimensions are the profile
# catalogue's (`elements/linear/profiles/01-ipe.json` to `13-chs.json`, read
# through `bim_profile_catalogue.dl`): depth h, width b, web tw, flange tf
# and root radius r (an angle's thickness as tw and tf; a hollow section's
# wall as tw and its outer corner radius, 1.5 t, as tf). This adds the whole
# European steel catalogue at once; the Profiles tab adds one profile when
# it is used (`add bim catalogue profile`).
import elements/linear/bim_profile_catalogue.dl

# The library loaded once: 1 at 2000100 of the project.
function bim steel library setting:
    replacement:
        2000100

# The steel profiles added to `target` as linear types, once (none when the
# library was loaded before), named by the rules once all are in. The ids
# made.
function add bim eu steel profiles to {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        set made to a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer
        if (the bim setting (bim steel library setting) of (0 as a 64 bit integer) in (@intrinsic("dereference", target)))'s found:
            return made
        # The European series of the profile catalogue, 1 IPE to 13 CHS,
        # appended directly; the rules name them all at the end.
        loop seriesCode from 1 to 14:
            set seriesProfiles to the bim catalogue profiles of series seriesCode
            loop profileCursor from 0 to the length of seriesProfiles:
                set catalogueProfile to the item at profileCursor in seriesProfiles
                loop roleCursor from 0 to 2:
                    set roleCode to bim beam role
                    if roleCursor = 1:
                        set roleCode to bim column role
                    if (roleCursor = 0) or catalogueProfile's columnToo:
                        set fresh to append bim catalogue profile catalogueProfile as role roleCode to target
                        if fresh != the bim refused id:
                            append fresh to (made's values)
            free seriesProfiles
        set bim setting (bim steel library setting) of (0 as a 64 bit integer) to (1 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
        name bim types by the rules in target
        return made
